|~ `::each`, the kind of a map in a shape whose values share one shape,
   and the laws declared under it.
   The decisions it exists for: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:each
  |~~ An each stands in the shape of a value for a map whose values all
      have one shape, the map a reader's data keys by names or ids:
      `{:alice {:id 1} :bob {:id 2}} | shape` answers
      `::shape::each{:id ::number}`, the one shape of every value standing for
      all of them and the keys left to the data, which `keys` reads. A map
      folds so where it holds more than one value, every value a map, a
      vector or a value under a tag, and all of one shape; a map of one
      key keeps it, a map of atoms keeps its keys, the fields a reader
      reads, `{:x 1 :y 2} | shape` answering
      `::shape{:x ::number :y ::number}`,
      and a map of values of other kinds, null among them, keeps its keys
      as well. A path of the data reads the shape past the
      key the fold stands for, `/alice/id` of the data `/id` of the shape,
      and a vector of such maps is `[::each{…}]`, a map of vectors
      `::each[…]`.
      ::link~(::any/shape | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :foldsAMapWhoseValuesShareOneShape
        |~~ A map whose values share one shape folds into an each. ~~|
        ~({:alice {:id 1} :bob {:id 2}} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:id ::number})
    | proves :readsThePathPastTheKey
        |~~ The path of the data reads the shape past the key it folds. ~~|
        ~({:alice {:id 1} :bob {:id 2}} | shape | get /id | eq ::number)
    | proves :foldsAMapOfValuesUnderOneTag
        |~~ A map of values under one tag folds into an each of the tag. ~~|
        ~({:alice ::user{:id 1} :bob ::user{:id 2}} | shape | eq ::shape::each::user)
    | proves :keepsTheFieldsOfAMapOfAtoms
        |~~ A map of atoms keeps its keys, the fields a reader reads. ~~|
        ~({:x 1 :y 2} | shape | eq ::shape{:x ::number :y ::number})
    | proves :keepsTheKeysOfValuesOfOtherKinds
        |~~ A map whose values part keeps its keys. ~~|
        ~({:a {:id 1} :b [1]} | shape | eq ::shape{:a {:id ::number} :b [::number]})
    | proves :keepsTheKeyOfAMapOfOne
        |~~ A map of one key keeps it. ~~|
        ~({:users [1]} | shape | eq ::shape{:users [::number]})
